{{also|thundër}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|thunder}}, {{m|enm|thonder}}, {{m|enm|thundre}}, {{m|enm|thonre}}, {{m|enm|thunnere}}, {{m|enm|þunre}}, from {{inh|en|ang|þunor|t=thunder}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*þunr}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*þunraz}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)ten-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(s)tenh₂-||to thunder}}.

Compare {{m|en|astound}}, {{m|en|astonish}}, {{m|en|stun}}. Germanic cognates include {{cog|fy|tonger}}, {{cog|nl|donder}}, {{cog|de|Donner}}, {{cog|non|Þórr}} ({{cog|en|Thor}}), {{cog|da|torden}}, {{cog|nn|tore}}. Other cognates include {{cog|fa|تندر|tr=tondar}}, {{cog|la|tonō}}, {{m|la|detonō}}, {{cog|grc|στένω}}, {{m|grc|στενάζω}}, {{m|grc|στόνος}}, {{m|grc|Στέντωρ}}, {{cog|ga|torann}}, {{cog|cy|taran}}, {{cog|cel-gau|Taranis}}. {{doublet|en|donner|Thunor|Thor}}.

