===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# The loud rumbling, cracking, or crashing [[sound]] caused by expansion of rapidly heated air around a [[lightning]] bolt.
#: {{ux|en|'''Thunder''' is preceded by lightning.}}
# A deep, [[rumble|rumbling]] noise resembling thunder.
#: {{ux|en|Off in the distance, he heard the '''thunder''' of hoofbeats, signalling a stampede.}}
# An alarming or startling [[threat]] or [[denunciation]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1847|author=w:William H. Prescott|title=A History of the Conquest of Peru
|passage=The '''thunders''' of the Vatican could no longer strike into the heart of princes.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The [[discharge]] of [[electricity]]; a [[thunderbolt]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King Lear|II|i|passage=The revenging gods / 'Gainst parricides did all their '''thunders''' bend.}}
# {{rfv-sense|en}} {{lb|en|figuratively}} The [[spotlight]].
#: {{ux|en|Shortly after I announced my pregnancy, he stole my '''thunder''' with his news of landing his dream job.}}
# {{lb|en|literature}} {{syn of|en|thunder word}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1996|author=William York Tindall|title=A Reader's Guide to Finnegans Wake|page=31
|passage=Adam's fall and Vico's thunder are embodied in a word of a hundred letters, the first of ten '''thunders''' in the Wake.}}

====Usage notes====
* [[roll]], [[clap]], [[peal]] are some of the words used to count thunder e.g. ''A series of rolls/claps/peals of thunder were heard''

